{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@ignite-ember/ui-react": ["../../../igni-sdk/packages/ui-react/src/index.ts"],
      "@ignite-ember/ui-react/*": ["../../../igni-sdk/packages/ui-react/src/*"],
      "@ignite-ember/test-utils/*": ["../../../igni-sdk/packages/test-utils/*"],
      "@ignite-ember/extension-bridge": ["../../../igni-sdk/packages/extension-bridge/src/index.ts"],
      "@ignite-ember/extension-bridge/*": ["../../../igni-sdk/packages/extension-bridge/src/*"],
      "@ignite-ember/ui-css": ["../../../igni-sdk/clients/ui/igni-ui.css"],
      /*
       * igni-sdk's ``packages/`` (at ``../igni-sdk``, beside this
       * repository: vite.config.ts says why) sit outside this directory,
       * so Node resolution walking up from them never reaches our
       * ``node_modules``. An extension author has these in their
       * own; here they have to be pointed at, or neither the example
       * nor the published floor can be type-checked at all.
       *
       * Listed one by one rather than with a `"*"` catch-all. The
       * catch-all is shorter and wrong: it wins over normal
       * resolution for every unmatched specifier, so it resolved
       * `react` to the untyped `index.js` instead of `@types/react`,
       * and bypassed the `types` field of packages that ship their
       * own. These are the floor's peers and the two test
       * libraries, which is the whole list.
       */
      "react": ["./node_modules/@types/react"],
      "react/*": ["./node_modules/@types/react/*"],
      "react-dom": ["./node_modules/@types/react-dom"],
      "react-dom/*": ["./node_modules/@types/react-dom/*"],
      "react-markdown": ["./node_modules/react-markdown"],
      "remark-gfm": ["./node_modules/remark-gfm"],
      "mermaid": ["./node_modules/mermaid"],
      "vitest": ["./node_modules/vitest"],
      "@testing-library/react": ["./node_modules/@testing-library/react"]
    },
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  /*
   * ``e2e`` is in here because it was not, and nothing noticed. F128.
   * Playwright transpiles each spec without type-checking it, so for as
   * long as this said ``["src"]`` the 48 e2e tests were the only
   * TypeScript in the repository that no compiler ever read — and three
   * of them do not run by default, so a type error in one of those was
   * invisible twice over.
   *
   * ``types`` is deliberately left unset: that pulls in every
   * ``@types/*`` package, which is how the specs get ``node:child_process``
   * without a second project. It also means app code can reach for
   * ``process`` — a real cost, and the reason the portal splits its
   * projects instead. Not worth the restructuring here while this
   * client's config is one flat project.
   */
  /*
   * The SDKs and their examples are type-checked in igni-sdk; what this
   * project reads of them is what ``paths`` points at.
   */
  "include": ["src", "e2e", "scripts"]
}
